iable heading"}, {"id": 49, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[68, 68]], "assertion": "outcome was defined as a binary indicator of any red card in the dyad", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["outcome variable"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 50, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[69, 69]], "assertion": "binary specification was chosen because red cards are rare, maximizing statistical power while preserving interpretability", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["outcome variable rationale"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 51, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[70, 71]], "note": "Exposure Variable heading"}, {"id": 52, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[72, 72]], "assertion": "dark skin defined as average rating ≥0.25 on a 0-1 scale", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["exposure definition"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 53, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[73, 73]], "assertion": "two independent raters coded skin tone from photos on a 5-point scale, converted to a 0-1 scale", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["skin tone measurement"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 54, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[74, 74]], "assertion": "inter-rater reliability: correlation 0.923, exact agreement 76.8%, agreement within 0.25 of 99.9%", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["inter-rater reliability"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 55, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[75, 75]], "assertion": "the two raters' scores were averaged", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["rater1", "rater2"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 56, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[76, 77]], "assertion": "the 0.25 dichotomization threshold was selected via exploratory specification search because it maximized the effect size (0.265pp unadjusted, 0.175pp adjusted)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["threshold selection"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [57]}, {"id": 57, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[76,